	<key>NSCalendarsFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DaGym keeps your scheduled workouts in a "DaGym" calendar of its own, so they show up alongside the rest of your day. It needs full access to update and remove the sessions it created when you change your plan; it never reads your other calendars.</string>
	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DaGym uses the camera to take progress photos, lined up with your previous shot, and to scan your gym membership card.</string>
	<key>NSFaceIDUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DaGym can lock your progress photos behind Face ID.</string>
	<key>NSHealthShareUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DaGym reads your bodyweight, body fat percentage, lean body mass, height, heart-rate variability, resting heart rate, sleep and workouts logged in other apps to personalise training suggestions and fill in your Body screen. What DaGym reads from Health stays on this iPhone — it is never copied to iCloud or sent to a server.</string>
	<key>NSHealthUpdateUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DaGym saves your strength workouts and bodyweight to Apple Health, plus an active-energy estimate only if you turn that on in Settings. Deleting a workout in DaGym deletes the one it wrote to Health too.</string>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DaGym uses the microphone so you can log sets by voice mid-workout. Audio is processed entirely on your device and never leaves it.</string>
	<key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DaGym can use an existing photo from your library as a progress photo.</string>
	<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription</key>
	<string>DaGym uses on-device speech recognition to turn what you say into a logged set. Nothing is sent to a server.</string>
	<key>NSSupportsLiveActivities</key>
	<true/>
	<key>NSSupportsLiveActivitiesFrequentUpdates</key>
